    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0499" n="1153" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1153"/>

                <head>No. 552.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Admiral Polo de
                    Bernabé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 28,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith for
                    your consideration a copy of the report<anchor n="*" xml:id="d253-f1"/> of a
                    naval court of inquiry convened under the direction of the President, by an
                    order of the Secretary of the Navy, promulgated on the 3d of January last, to
                    inquire into the causes of the foundering of the steamer Virginius, then
                    recently delivered to the United States by order of the government of Spain.</p>
                <p>The report contains all the evidence, documentary and oral, submitted to the
                    court of inquiry in relation to the subject of the inquiry on that occasion.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
